{"id":"u-4fa965b4-afcb-4ab5-ab74-e26058cc4be9","src":"community","title":"Broly","author":"Jaron Z.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/broly-54","desc":"This program is designed to build as much muscle as possible, while gaining strength.\n\n-You can go 6 days in a row, or 3 on 1 off if you need an extra rest day. \n\n-Don't worry about trying to hit the top end of the rep ranges, just make sure your reps don't fall below the minimum rep range. \n\n-There should be some rep dropoff set to set. If your reps don't drop from the 1st set vs the last set, you're not training close enough to failure.\n\n-Each week try to add 5-10 pounds to compound lifts (2.5 pounds for isolations) and match reps from the previous week's session. OR beat your reps by 1 from the previous week's session, with the same weight from the previous week.\n\nExample:\nLast week on bench press you did 100lbs for 12 reps, on set 1. This week you will need to hit 105-110lbs for 12 reps, OR 100 for 13 reps, to progress.\n\nNote: *The first set of each exercise is the one you're trying to match/beat reps from the previous week. This is how you're going to gauge performance. \nMatching subsequent sets isn't as important, although performance should be similar to the previous week's session.*\n\n*If you're unable to match, or beat reps, stick with the same weight next week, until you can beat your reps; then repeat.\n\n-If you're feeling too beat up; or if your performance drops significantly for 2 or 3 sessions, take 3 rest days in a row. If you need to do this, repeat the previous week, then try progressing again.","level":["Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":70,"joins":371,"rate":5,"rateCount":1,"updated":"2026-10-31T22:16:35.143Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Chest and Back","Arms Focused","Quad Focused Lower","Back Focused","Shoulders and Arms","'Hinge' Focused lower"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Close Grip)","sets":[{"